+# The Specialty Filter Folds Case in the Query, Not in the Schema
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+`REQ-VET-003` and `REQ-VET-004` require the Specialty filter to match a whole name, disregarding letter case, on both forms of the Veterinarian directory.
+
+The one precedent in this codebase reaches case-insensitivity through the database. Owner search relies on per-vendor column behavior: H2 types the column `VARCHAR_IGNORECASE`, MySQL uses a case-insensitive collation, and PostgreSQL does neither. The same search therefore returns different results per vendor, recorded in [system-design.md § Known Defects](../system-design.md#known-defects).
+
+The Specialty filter must not inherit that divergence. It must match identically on all three supported vendors.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Rely on column collation, as owner search does.** Rejected: it reproduces the recorded vendor divergence in a second feature.
+2. **Change the three `specialties` schemas so each folds case.** Rejected: the hand-maintained per-vendor schemas are the root cause of the existing defect.
+3. **Fold case in the query** (chosen): the derived query carries the `IgnoreCase` keyword, which every vendor evaluates the same way.
+
+## Decision
+
+The Specialty filter folds case in the query. The schema and seed files are unchanged.
+
+Both surfaces call the same repository finder, so the page and the machine-readable directory cannot diverge in what they match.
+
+This decision does not repair owner search. That defect stays open and is unrelated to this slice.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Matching is vendor-independent, so the H2-backed test suite is evidence for MySQL and PostgreSQL too.
+- The comparison wraps the joined column, which a plain index on the specialty name cannot serve. Specialties are a three-row lookup table, so the cost is not material.
+- A future filter over a large table needs its own decision; this one does not generalize by size.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003, REQ-VET-004
+
+- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/vet/VetRepository.java` — the finders that carry the match.
+- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/vet/VetController.java` — both surfaces call them.
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Persistence](../system-design.md#persistence) — where the vendor case-handling differences are recorded.
+- [The non-goal ADR narrowing NG-9](2026-08-11-non-goal-vet-search-narrowed.md) — why the filter is in scope at all.
