+# Specialty-Filtered Veterinarian Reads Are Not Cached
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The two unfiltered `VetRepository` reads are annotated `@Cacheable("vets")`. The `vets` cache is declared with statistics enabled and nothing else: no size limit, no eviction, no expiry. [system-design.md § Open Questions](../system-design.md#open-questions-from-the-survey) records the missing eviction as unsettled.
+
+Today every key in that cache comes from the application. The no-argument read keys on nothing; the paged read keys on a page request the controller builds.
+
+The Specialty filter changes that. Its finders take a name supplied by the caller, on routes that require no authentication. Caching them would let any caller mint cache entries, one per distinct string, against a cache with no bound.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Annotate the filtered finders too, for symmetry with the unfiltered pair.** Rejected: it puts an unbounded, caller-controlled key set into an unbounded cache.
+2. **Cache them behind a second, separately bounded cache.** Rejected: sizing and eviction are the open question, and this slice does not settle it.
+3. **Leave the filtered finders uncached** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+`@Cacheable` stays on the unfiltered reads only. The `vets` cache continues to hold only entries whose keys the application controls.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- No caller can grow the cache. The change leaves the application no weaker than its recorded baseline.
+- Every filtered request reaches the database. The Veterinarian directory is small and the query is a single join, so the read cost is acceptable.
+- Symmetry within `VetRepository` is broken: two annotated methods beside two unannotated ones. This ADR is the reason a reader will look for.
+- Caching filtered reads stays available once eviction and sizing are decided.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003, REQ-VET-004
+
+- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/vet/VetRepository.java` — where the annotations are, and are not.
+- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/system/CacheConfiguration.java` — the cache declaration this decision reads.
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the recorded cache scope.
